-- tests-independent-2.l4: assertions written by an independent test author from lead/answers.md, written before the deposit was opened.
-- Every expected value is the one in answers.md for the block named in the comment above the assertion, never the encoding's own output.
-- Where a seat function asks the converse of a block, or reports compliance where the block asks "must I", a `note` comment above the assertion says how the block's answer was translated.
-- A block that no function asks is a comment line "-- <id>: no function asks this (<why>)".
-- This file: the K2 range, then Chapter III.


-- K2-001
-- note: polarity: the function asks the converse of the block (the block asks "may I / am I entitled", the function "is it barred / does it not apply"); the block's no is JUST TRUE here, the block's yes is JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 1(3), as a controller, is a restriction or prohibition of the free movement of the personal data I process within the Union barred when its reason is the protection of natural persons` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- K2-002
-- note: polarity: the function asks the converse of the block (the block asks "may I / am I entitled", the function "is it barred / does it not apply"); the block's no is JUST TRUE here, the block's yes is JUST FALSE
